   "If an entire `g` agrees off a compact set with a transform satisfying `z·g(z) → L ≠ 0`, divide by `z` to get `g(z) → 0`; Liouville then forces `g = 0`, contradicting uniqueness of the first limit."
   :how-to-apply
   ["Turn equality outside a compact set into `g =ᶠ[cocompact ℂ] f` using the compact set's complement as a cocompact neighbourhood."
    "Transport the known limit of `z * f z` to `z * g z` with an explicit eventual equality and `Filter.Tendsto.congr'`."
    "Prove `z⁻¹ → 0` along `cocompact ℂ` from `tendsto_norm_cocompact_atTop`."
    "Away from the singleton `{0}`, rewrite `g z = z⁻¹ * (z * g z)` and conclude `g z → 0`."
    "Apply `Differentiable.apply_eq_of_tendsto_cocompact` to the entire function and obtain `g = 0` everywhere."
    "The zero function makes `z * g z → 0`; use uniqueness of limits against the transported nonzero limit."
    "Discharge nonzeroness from the positive-measure hypothesis on the original compact set."]
   :problem-class
   "Show a Cauchy transform of a positive-measure compact real set cannot agree with an entire function outside its singular support."
   :proof-shape
   {:eventual-agreement
    "EqOn outside a compact image becomes EventuallyEq along `cocompact ℂ`."
    :decay
    "`z*g(z) → -volume(K)` and `z⁻¹ → 0` imply `g(z) → 0`."
    :rigidity
    "Liouville turns cocompact decay of an entire function into global zero."
    :contradiction
    "The same function `z*g(z)` cannot tend both to zero and to the nonzero value `-volume(K)`."}
